IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `roc-core`
IMPORT `roc12-order-68`

-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore) -- tests for Order 68 (roc12-order-68.l4).
-- Every expected value is written from the text of the Rule (lines 7662 to 7675 of the source file) before the run.
-- Line 7671, paragraph (2)(4), is "[ Deleted by S 174/2026 wef 01/04/2026 ]" and has no function to test.

§ `O 68 r 1`
#ASSERT `o 68 r 1 the enactment is the Act` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- ""Act" means the Variable Capital Companies Act 2018"
#ASSERT `o 68 r 1 the enactment is the Act` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "means"
#ASSERT `o 68 r 1 a thing is a sub-fund` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- the meaning given by section 2(1) is passed through
#ASSERT `o 68 r 1 a thing is a sub-fund` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- likewise
#ASSERT `o 68 r 1 a thing is a sub-fund` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING -- the Act is not among the sources
#ASSERT `o 68 r 1 a company is a VCC` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- the meaning given by section 2(1) is passed through
#ASSERT `o 68 r 1 a company is a VCC` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING -- the Act is not among the sources

§ `O 68 r 2`
-- r 2(1).  Arguments: an application under the Act; the Act or this Order provides otherwise.
#ASSERT `o 68 r 2(1) the requirement to apply by originating application applies` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- every application under the Act, nothing provided otherwise
#ASSERT `o 68 r 2(1) the requirement to apply by originating application applies` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "Unless otherwise provided in the Act or this Order"
#ASSERT `o 68 r 2(1) the requirement to apply by originating application applies` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not an application under the Act: outside the scope
-- Arguments: the answer above; made by originating application.
#ASSERT `o 68 r 2(1) the application is made by originating application as the Rule requires` (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- by originating application
#ASSERT `o 68 r 2(1) the application is made by originating application as the Rule requires` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- QB: made another way
#ASSERT `o 68 r 2(1) the application is made by originating application as the Rule requires` (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- QD: the requirement does not apply
#ASSERT `o 68 r 2(1) the application is made by originating application as the Rule requires` NOTHING TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- whether the requirement applies is not answered
-- r 2(2).
#ASSERT `o 68 r 2(2) the application may be made by originating application without notice` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "An application under section 156 may be made by originating application without notice"
#ASSERT `o 68 r 2(2) the application may be made by originating application without notice` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- a permission for section 156 applications says nothing of others
-- r 2(3).  Arguments: an application under s 216 of the Companies Act as applied by s 142; made by originating claim.
#ASSERT `o 68 r 2(3) the application is made by originating claim as the Rule requires` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- by originating claim
#ASSERT `o 68 r 2(3) the application is made by originating claim as the Rule requires` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- QB: made another way
#ASSERT `o 68 r 2(3) the application is made by originating claim as the Rule requires` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- not a section 216 application

§ `O 68 r 3`
-- r 3(1).  Arguments: an originating application or other document to which the Order relates; entitled in the matter of the VCC; entitled in the matter of the Act.
#ASSERT `o 68 r 3(1) the document is entitled as the Rule requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- entitled in the matter of the VCC and the Act
#ASSERT `o 68 r 3(1) the document is entitled as the Rule requires` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- QB: not entitled in the matter of the VCC
#ASSERT `o 68 r 3(1) the document is entitled as the Rule requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- QB: not entitled in the matter of the Act
#ASSERT `o 68 r 3(1) the document is entitled as the Rule requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- a document outside the Rule
-- r 3(2).  Arguments: a section 58(6) application; a VCC of conviction exists; entitled in the matter of that VCC; entitled in the matter of the Act.
#ASSERT `o 68 r 3(2) the originating application is entitled as the Rule requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- entitled in the matter of the VCC of conviction and the Act
#ASSERT `o 68 r 3(2) the originating application is entitled as the Rule requires` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- no such VCC: "(if any)"
#ASSERT `o 68 r 3(2) the originating application is entitled as the Rule requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- QB: the VCC exists and is not named
#ASSERT `o 68 r 3(2) the originating application is entitled as the Rule requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- QB: not entitled in the matter of the Act
#ASSERT `o 68 r 3(2) the originating application is entitled as the Rule requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- not a section 58(6) application

§ `O 68 r 4`
#ASSERT `o 68 r 4 the Court may by order give such direction as it thinks fit` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- at the first case conference on an application to which the Order relates
#ASSERT `o 68 r 4 the Court may by order give such direction as it thinks fit` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- another occasion: "Without limiting Order 9"
#ASSERT `o 68 r 4 the Court may by order give such direction as it thinks fit` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- an application to which the Order does not relate

§ `O 68 -- the duties as regulative rules`
-- expected: FULFILLED
#TRACE `o 68 r 3(1) the duty to entitle the document` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 68 the person who files the document` DOES `o 68 entitle the document in the matter of the VCC and of the Act` AT 1
